2026-03-29T07:29:59 The text leading up to this was:
2026-03-29T07:29:59 --------------------------
2026-03-29T07:29:59 |From fd848f0d43b843c66aaf43c2861ba8e31cebc1e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
2026-03-29T07:29:59 |From: bluhm <bluhm@openbsd.org>
2026-03-29T07:29:59 |Date: Sat, 8 Jul 2023 14:49:55 +0000
2026-03-29T07:29:59 |Subject: [PATCH] Fix Perl tests in OpenBSD regress.
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |Disable Perl test t/porting/exec-bit.t as it only checks permissions.
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |The x-bit in OpenBSD CVS tree does not match Perl distribution tar.
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |This is known and accepted.
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |Set permission of Test-Harness source.sh and source_args.sh to
2026-03-29T07:30:00 |executable as Perl uses it to test module features. Stay close to
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |upstream. During regress, set the x-bit of the files in obj
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |directory. Do not touch src tree, it might be read-only.
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |discussed with anton@; OK afresh1@
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |--- Plus this patch to the regress suite
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#diff --git a/regress/gnu/usr.bin/perl/Makefile b/regress/gnu/usr.bin/perl/Makefile
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#index 9ca83dee61a..56ebf47f2fc 100644
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#--- a/regress/gnu/usr.bin/perl/Makefile
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#+++ b/regress/gnu/usr.bin/perl/Makefile
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
2026-03-29T07:30:01 |#-# $OpenBSD: Makefile,v 1.3 2023/07/05 21:38:22 bluhm Exp $
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#+# $OpenBSD: Makefile,v 1.4 2023/07/08 14:49:55 bluhm Exp $
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |# .if ! (make(clean) || make(cleandir) || make(obj))
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |# NCPU != /sbin/sysctl -n hw.ncpuonline
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#@@ -12,13 +12,17 @@ build:
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |# REGRESS_SETUP += permissions
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |# permissions:
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#- # The permissions in CVS tree are not as in the Perl distribution.
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#- # Match expectations of t/porting/exec-bit.t and
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#- # cpan/Test-Harness/t/source_tests/source.sh
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#- awk '{print $$1}' ${BSDSRCDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/MANIFEST ||#- ( cd ${BSDOBJDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/ && xargs chmod -x )
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#- grep -v '^#' ${BSDSRCDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/Porting/exec-bit.txt ||#- ( cd ${BSDOBJDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/ && xargs chmod +x )
2026-03-29T07:30:02 |#+ # Permissions in CVS src tree are not as in the Perl distribution.
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ # Match expectations of cpan/Test-Harness/t/source_handler.t for
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ # cpan/Test-Harness/t/source_tests/source*.sh executalbe bits.
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ # Remove symlink and fix permissions of copy in obj directory.
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+.for f in |#+ cpan/Test-Harness/t/source_tests/source.sh |#+ cpan/Test-Harness/t/source_tests/source_args.sh
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ rm -f ${BSDOBJDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/$f
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ cp ${BSDSRCDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/$f ${BSDOBJDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/$f
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+ chmod +x ${BSDOBJDIR}/gnu/usr.bin/perl/$f
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#+.endfor
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |#
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |# REGRESS_TARGETS += test
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |# test:
2026-03-29T07:30:03 |---
2026-03-29T07:30:03 | gnu/usr.bin/perl/t/porting/exec-bit.t | 4 ++++
